# The build context: the workspace manifests and lockfile, all of crates/ (sources, build
# scripts, examples, tests and fixtures: Cargo loads every target a manifest declares, and
# crates/pinakes-core declares the e2e_stack example), the compile-time inputs in data/
# and migrations/, and LICENSE with the script that writes the third-party notices and its
# licence texts (scripts/spdx/).
# Everything else stays out: local config, .env files, target/, e2e/, docs.
# A rule for a directory covers everything below it; test_contracts.py checks every rule.
**
!Cargo.toml
!Cargo.lock
!LICENSE
!crates/
!data/
!migrations/
!scripts/third-party-notices
!scripts/spdx/
